637
00:49:17.290 --> 00:49:20.283
See, I knew no one would believe
me unless I got it on Memorex.

638
00:49:29.890 --> 00:49:31.690
What exactly am I supposed to be
listening to?

639
00:49:33.130 --> 00:49:35.964
The people under the floor,
dude.

640
00:49:36.010 --> 00:49:37.205
The aliens.

641
00:49:38.690 --> 00:49:41.000
They're there.

642
00:49:41.050 --> 00:49:44.282
Well, yeah, it is strange.

643
00:49:44.330 --> 00:49:46.970
But it's probably
geothermal activity

644
00:49:47.010 --> 00:49:48.649
- or magnetic distortions.
- No, no.

645
00:49:48.690 --> 00:49:49.885
Something like that.

646
00:49:49.930 --> 00:49:51.330
They came on the rock.

647
00:49:51.370 --> 00:49:56.161
Look, no offense, Ezra,
but that's pretty out there.

648
00:49:56.210 --> 00:49:58.247
You don't get it, do you?

649
00:49:58.290 --> 00:50:01.681
It's not out there.
It's in here.

650
00:50:02.450 --> 00:50:04.919
It's in the static.
It's in the moisture.

651
00:50:04.970 --> 00:50:07.166
Up is down.
Fast is slow.

652
00:50:07.210 --> 00:50:10.123
What's in here is out there,

653
00:50:10.170 --> 00:50:12.366
and what's out there
is in here now.

654
00:50:12.410 --> 00:50:13.969
Comprendo?

655
00:50:15.770 --> 00:50:18.808
Um, look,

656
00:50:18.850 --> 00:50:21.066
why don't you think about
getting out of here for a while?

657
00:50:21.090 --> 00:50:22.410
I'm gonna be back tomorrow.

658
00:50:22.450 --> 00:50:23.930
I'll have some more equipment
with me.

659
00:50:23.970 --> 00:50:26.439
I'm sure it will all make
more sense in the morning.

660
00:50:26.490 --> 00:50:28.402
Morning?

661
00:50:28.450 --> 00:50:30.123
Dude, it's already morning.

662
00:50:32.210 --> 00:50:34.600
All right. Um, stick to
bottled water, okay?

663
00:50:40.810 --> 00:50:43.370
Oh, hey, I will let you know
if I see G-spot.

664
00:50:44.610 --> 00:50:47.364
You might see her, but I don't
think you'll recognize her.

665
00:50:56.370 --> 00:50:57.645
Nathan.

666
00:51:01.450 --> 00:51:03.169
Doing okay?
We're almost there.

667
00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:05.486
Yeah.
I just feel so stupid.

668
00:51:05.530 --> 00:51:07.999
I mean, I just don't even know
what I was thinking.

669
00:51:12.330 --> 00:51:14.526
And I don't even want to
think about

670
00:51:14.570 --> 00:51:19.361
how many clients I pissed off
by not getting back to them.

671
00:51:19.410 --> 00:51:21.845
- Mm.
- The surgery was successful.

672
00:51:21.890 --> 00:51:23.210
That's the important thing.

673
00:51:23.250 --> 00:51:24.889
Look out!
Aah!

674
00:51:31.210 --> 00:51:32.746
- Christ, that was close.
- What... What...

675
00:51:32.770 --> 00:51:34.807
Did you see that thing?
What was that thing?

676
00:51:34.850 --> 00:51:37.649
- Did you see its eyes?
- Oh, my God.

677
00:51:37.690 --> 00:51:39.921
What are you doing?

678
00:51:39.970 --> 00:51:43.008
I-I want to call the kids,
just check that they're okay.

679
00:51:43.050 --> 00:51:44.370
Honey, the kids are fine.

680
00:53:45.570 --> 00:53:47.846
What are you doing
in my room?

681
00:53:47.890 --> 00:53:50.485
- Where have you been?
- I was out in the back field.

682
00:53:50.530 --> 00:53:55.161
I thought I heard Sam.
I was worried about him.

683
00:53:55.210 --> 00:53:56.849
Look, I know it sounds weird,

684
00:53:56.890 --> 00:53:59.689
but I kind of got lost
out there.

685
00:53:59.770 --> 00:54:01.410
You know, like,
one second it was daytime,

686
00:54:01.450 --> 00:54:03.885
then all of a sudden
it was so dark

687
00:54:03.930 --> 00:54:05.284
I couldn't even
find the house.

688
00:54:09.450 --> 00:54:12.363
What the hell is going on?

689
00:54:12.410 --> 00:54:14.845
It's probably Dad.

690
00:54:14.890 --> 00:54:16.688
At least I hope it's Dad.

691
00:54:23.410 --> 00:54:26.050
Dad?

692
00:54:30.810 --> 00:54:31.926
Who was that?

693
00:54:33.930 --> 00:54:35.000
I'm not sure.

694
00:54:36.930 --> 00:54:38.159
Christ, now what?

695
00:54:40.490 --> 00:54:41.490
Wait, where's Jack?

696
00:54:57.610 --> 00:54:59.570
Baby, what are you doing
out here all by yourself?

697
00:54:59.610 --> 00:55:01.602
Mommy!

698
00:55:01.650 --> 00:55:03.687
- Jack.
- Jack!

699
00:55:03.770 --> 00:55:05.807
Oh, my God.

700
00:55:05.850 --> 00:55:08.285
What is wrong
with you two?

701
00:55:08.330 --> 00:55:10.049
Why is your brother out here
by himself?

702
00:55:10.090 --> 00:55:12.266
- No, it didn't happen that way.
- What is this?

703
00:55:12.290 --> 00:55:14.122
While the cat's away,
the mice will play?

704
00:55:14.170 --> 00:55:15.570
Isn't that right?

705
00:55:15.610 --> 00:55:17.226
I'm seriously disappointed
in both of you.

706
00:55:17.250 --> 00:55:19.845
No, there was this sound,
and I got sick,

707
00:55:19.890 --> 00:55:22.450
and then you called
and yelled at me.

708
00:55:22.490 --> 00:55:25.289
Honey, what are you
talking about?

709
00:55:25.330 --> 00:55:27.765
We couldn't even get through,
and believe me, we tried.

710
00:55:27.810 --> 00:55:29.666
She's telling the truth, Dad.
Something weird is going on.

711
00:55:29.690 --> 00:55:32.330
I don't want to hear
your excuses either, Benny.

712
00:55:32.370 --> 00:55:33.804
I'm gonna take him upstairs.

713
00:55:33.850 --> 00:55:36.888
I'll leave you
to deal with these two.

714
00:55:36.930 --> 00:55:38.649
Holy shit.

715
00:55:40.450 --> 00:55:42.760
They should have been put back
in the barn hours ago.

716
00:55:42.810 --> 00:55:44.266
You haven't even fed them yet,
have you?

717
00:55:44.290 --> 00:55:47.124
- Dad, I tried, but...
- What do you mean, you tried?

718
00:55:47.170 --> 00:55:50.561
Do you have any idea
how much those animals cost us?

719
00:55:50.610 --> 00:55:52.841
They are alpacas!

720
00:55:52.890 --> 00:55:54.244
Alpacas.

721
00:55:55.930 --> 00:55:56.930
Dad...

722
00:56:04.490 --> 00:56:06.925
I mean, should we, like,
try to warn him.

723
00:56:10.050 --> 00:56:12.770
Warn him about what?

724
00:56:19.530 --> 00:56:20.759
Sam?

725
00:56:20.810 --> 00:56:23.928
Come on.
Come on.

726
00:56:23.970 --> 00:56:26.405
Sam?
Here, boy.

727
00:56:29.970 --> 00:56:32.644
Stupid goddamn dog.

728
00:56:32.690 --> 00:56:34.886
You too, huh?

729
00:56:34.930 --> 00:56:37.570
You know,
if I could just get

730
00:56:37.610 --> 00:56:40.444
a little consideration
around here,

731
00:56:40.490 --> 00:56:42.004
just a little support,

732
00:56:42.050 --> 00:56:45.202
it would be
greatly fucking appreciated.

733
00:56:55.770 --> 00:56:58.763
Dad's acting weird, right?

734
00:56:58.810 --> 00:57:00.085
You noticed?

735
00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:07.250
Where's Sam?

736
00:57:09.250 --> 00:57:11.048
T-They must have got him.

737
00:57:11.090 --> 00:57:12.604
They?

738
00:57:12.650 --> 00:57:15.165
Uh, what the fuck
are you talking about?

739
00:57:16.370 --> 00:57:18.043
They, them, it.

740
00:57:18.090 --> 00:57:20.127
That thing that has been
fucking this place up.

741
00:57:20.170 --> 00:57:21.240
I mean, come on, Dad.

742
00:57:21.290 --> 00:57:22.586
Don't pretend that
you haven't noticed.

743
00:57:22.610 --> 00:57:25.489
Nothing has been
fucking this place up.

744
00:57:25.530 --> 00:57:27.886
Why are you so in denial?

745
00:57:27.930 --> 00:57:31.844
Okay, you know, I've had it
with your drama, Lavinia,

746
00:57:31.890 --> 00:57:35.088
so do me a favor and get
the fuck out of my sight, okay?

747
00:57:35.130 --> 00:57:38.043
No, no, actually,
I'll save you the trouble

748
00:57:38.090 --> 00:57:40.366
and get the fuck
out of yours!

749
00:57:43.890 --> 00:57:45.244
Look, he doesn't mean it.

750
00:57:48.810 --> 00:57:53.089
Do you still have
that girlfriend in Aylesbury?

751
00:57:53.130 --> 00:57:54.564
Well, she wasn't
my girlfriend,

752
00:57:54.610 --> 00:57:56.886
and I haven't seen her
in months.

753
00:57:56.930 --> 00:57:59.047
Why?

754
00:57:59.090 --> 00:58:04.290
Because we need to get
the hell out of here.

755
00:58:06.170 --> 00:58:07.240
Look.

756
00:58:07.290 --> 00:58:09.759
Make him really scary.

757
00:58:09.810 --> 00:58:10.810
Oh, yes.

758
00:58:12.770 --> 00:58:14.841
What?

759
00:58:14.890 --> 00:58:16.847
Uh, are you okay?

760
00:58:16.890 --> 00:58:19.007
No, I just blew up
at Lavinia.

761
00:58:19.050 --> 00:58:21.770
I don't think I'll be winning
any "father of the year" awards.

762
00:58:21.810 --> 00:58:24.644
Oh, she's that age.
